  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "L1 gold records uniformly report human oral bioavailability below 20% for all reference contexts: tegaserod ~10% fasted (C01, C06, C18, C22), epanolol 5.85–7.89% across fasted/fed solution/tablet (C02, C04, C08, C11, C14, C21), aliskiren 2–5% (C05, C13, C17, C20), alvimopan 6% (C09, C10, C16, C19), melagatran 3–7% fasted and 0.9% fed (C07, C15), argatroban poor (C03), and CDP323 14% (C12).",
      "card_ids": ["C01","C02","C03","C04","C05","C06","C07","C08","C09","C10","C11","C12","C13","C14","C15","C16","C17","C18","C19","C20","C21","C22"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L2 context reinforces the low-F direction for polar/peptidic molecules: argatroban and related peptidomimetics are not orally bioavailable due to poor enteral absorption and presystemic hepatic extraction (C25, C28, C35); aliskiren's low F is linked to intestinal P-gp efflux (C34); alvimopan is poor in dogs (C24); tegaserod remains ~10% (C27, C30).",
      "card_ids": ["C24","C25","C27","C28","C30","C34","C35"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 permeability records for peptide/peptidomimetic reference molecules show low intestinal permeability: DADLE P_B 2.46×10^-7 cm/s and Caco-2 AP-BL 7.80×10^-8 cm/s (C52, C59); FMLP Papp 1.3×10^-7 cm/s (C54); hexarelin Papp <1.5 to 6×10^-7 cm/s depending on formulation (C49, C51, C53, C55, C57); prodrug 1 Papp 1.80×10^-8 cm/s (C58).",
      "card_ids": ["C48","C49","C50","C51","C52","C53","C54","C55","C56","C57","C58","C59"]
    },
