      "claim": "L5 gut-wall/efflux records mostly show very low absorptive permeability or efflux-dominated transport for peptide/macrocyclic references: MC-LR A-B 0.3–1.4% of loaded amount over 24 h and Papp AB 2.4×10^-8 cm/s with BA 4.0×10^-8 cm/s (C61, C63, C67, C70); DG013A A-B <1.0×10^-6 cm/s with B-A below LOQ (C62); compounds 25/26 A-B 0.28/0.16×10^-6 cm/s (C60, C64); indinavir mouse ileum <1.5% absorbed (C65).",
      "card_ids": ["C60","C61","C62","C63","C64","C65","C67","C70"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 hepatic clearance/metabolic stability records provide mechanistic context for presystemic loss but are not query-specific: compound 5 showed only 4% recovery after 30 min in rat liver microsomes (C76), and peptide-like references showed measurable HLM intrinsic clearance (C79, C83); CYP-contribution records for ritonavir/bortezomib (C73-C75, C77, C78, C80, C81) are small and not directly transferable.",
      "card_ids": ["C72","C76","C79","C83"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Some L6 records show moderate metabolic stability or small CYP contributions (KZR-616 HLM half-life 76 min, C82; ritonavir CYP2J2 2–7%, C73/C78/C80; bortezomib CYP contributions 1.2–6.6%, C74/C75/C77/C81), but these are for unrelated molecules and do not provide affirmative evidence for query F ≥ 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C73","C74","C75","C77","C78","C80","C81","C82"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The query's physicochemical profile (MW 4113 Da, TPSA 1646 Å², logD -19.4, 57 HBD, 56 HBA, 149 rotatable bonds, fully ionized, 7 carboxylic acids, 2 guanidines, 34 secondary amides) coherently supports negligible membrane permeability and F < 20%; no affirmative evidence supports F ≥ 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C01","C02","C05","C09","C15","C21","C52","C54","C58","C60","C61","C62","C64","C65","C67","C70","C76"]
    }
  ],
