      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C72","C76","C79","C83"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct measured oral bioavailability for the query molecule itself; all F values come from structurally different small-molecule contexts.",
    "No query-specific oral vs IV exposure, permeability, solubility, or first-pass data are supplied.",
    "L6 hepatic clearance/metabolic stability records are for unrelated reference molecules, not the query, and are not direct F measurements; no query-specific proteolytic stability or hepatocyte clearance data are available.",
    "No formulation or absorption-enhancer context is supplied for the query.",
    "Active transport or specialized delivery cannot be fully excluded from visible evidence, though none is indicated."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L1 gold records uniformly report human oral bioavailability below 20%; L2 context reinforces low F for polar/peptidic molecules; L4 permeability records for peptide-like references show low intestinal permeability; L5 gut-wall/efflux records mostly show very low absorptive permeability or efflux-dominated transport; L6 hepatic clearance/metabolic stability records add mechanistic plausibility for presystemic loss but are not query-specific. The query's extreme size, polarity, and ionization coherently support F < 20%; no affirmative evidence supports F ≥ 20%, so the prediction remains low with high confidence."
